translated_text:
Article 3

(1) The objective of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence is to provide protection and services to victims of violence based on gender and the best interests of women and children occurring at home and/or in public places.

(21 Violence as referred to in paragraph (1)

can be in the form of: n

a. physical violence;

b. psychological violence;

c. sexual violence;

d. economic neglect; and

e. restriction of movement.

